    <string name="backup_start">备份</string>
    <!--
      The consequence a deterministic file name has and nothing else on the sheet names: an archive is
      <package>-<versionCode>.thorbak, so backing the same app up twice at the same version always
      collides.

      This used to read "can replace the backup you already have", because the three destinations
      genuinely disagreed: MediaStore de-duplicates to "name (1)", a SAF provider usually does, and a
      legacy Downloads write renamed straight over the old file. AppArchiveStoreImpl now picks a
      non-colliding name on that third backend too (nonCollidingArchiveName), so "kept alongside" is
      the behaviour Thor itself produces everywhere.

      The hedge survives, narrowed to the one case Thor does not control: a folder the user chose is
      the provider's to manage, and DocumentsContract.renameDocument onto an existing name is the
      provider's decision. Promising "never replaces" would be a claim Thor cannot honour there.

      Stated before the button rather than as an "are you sure?", which is the branch's rule for
      destructive actions: name the consequence, do not ask the user to confirm a sentence they have
      not been given.
    -->
    <string name="backup_overwrite_notice">Thor 以应用及其版本为备份命名，因此在同一版本下再次备份此应用会重复使用该名称。Thor 会给较新的一个加上编号，从而两个都保留；但你自己选择的文件夹可能会改为替换较旧的文件。</string>
    <!--
      Shown when every data class is unticked. Its second sentence is the whole of C1: the restore gate
      refuses an empty selection before it looks at the installer, so an installer-only archive is a
      file Thor can write and can never read back. The sheet used to offer exactly that.
    -->
    <string name="backup_nothing_selected">请至少选择一项要备份的内容。仅有安装包是无法恢复的。</string>
    <string name="backup_done">备份已保存。</string>
    <string name="backup_failed">备份失败：%1$s</string>
    <string name="backup_failed_unknown">它没有说明原因就停止了</string>
    <!--
      The backup counterpart of restore_failed_partial, and deliberately not a copy of it: a backup
      reads the app's data and writes somewhere else, so there is no half-written app to warn about.
      What the user needs is the other half — that no archive was left behind either. That is true by
      construction rather than by hope: AppArchiveStoreImpl writes to <name>.part and only publishes on
      success, discards the partial on failure, and sweeps orphaned ones at the next launch.
    -->
    <string name="backup_failed_nothing_saved">未保存任何备份文件。应用自身的数据未被改动——备份只会读取它。</string>
    <!--
      The pre-flight failures: the enqueue returned no id, or something between the passphrase recall
      and the enqueue threw. Both are decided before a job exists.
    -->
    <string name="backup_failed_not_started">未开始任何操作，因此未保存任何备份。</string>
    <!--
      Cancelled without ever running — the chain case, matching restore_cancelled. Every job is appended
      to one chain and WorkManager cancels the dependents of a job that fails, so a backup queued behind
      a failing one is cancelled before its work is ever called. Reported as its own outcome rather than
      as a failure: "Backup failed" over a backup Thor never attempted is a sentence the user cannot act
      on, and the action here is simply to try again.
    -->
    <string name="backup_cancelled">Thor 没有运行这次备份——队列中排在它前面的任务失败了，因此这次备份在开始前就被取消。未保存任何备份。请重试。</string>
    <string name="backup_cancelled_after_start">这次备份在已经开始之后被取消。</string>
    <!--
      Its own string rather than restore_interrupted_dismiss, which is named and commented for the §8.5
      breadcrumb banner. Identical text today; rewording one must not silently reword the other.
    -->
    <string name="backup_outcome_dismiss">知道了</string>
    <!--
      One word, because it is the label the sheet's running frame is built around: while a job is live
      the sheet shows the bar and this button and nothing else. It dismisses the sheet, which is safe
      for the reason the sentence below states — the job is a foreground service and the sheet is only
      watching it.
    -->
    <string name="backup_background">后台运行</string>
    <string name="backup_background_desc">关闭此界面后它仍会继续运行。通知会显示进度。</string>

    <string name="restore_title">恢复备份</string>
